nd 729 using the distributive property is 6975712.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! Using the distributive property simplifies the multiplication process by breaking it down into smaller, more manageable parts. The final answer remains the same, 6975712. If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Can you provide an example of how to solve this problem using the area model for multiplication?\n<think>\nCertainly! The area model for multiplication is a visual method that helps break down the multiplication of two numbers into smaller, more manageable parts. We can use the area model to multiply 968 and 729 by dividing each number into its place values and then finding the area of each rectangle formed by these divisions. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n<answer>\nTo solve the multiplication of 968 and 729 using the area model, we'll first express each number in terms of its place values:\n968 = 900 + 60 + 8\n729 = 700 + 20 + 9\nNow, we'll create a rectangle and divide it into smaller rectangles based on these place values. The area of each smaller rectangle will represent the product of the corresponding place values. Let's draw the area model:\n```\n      900 | 60 | 8\n      ----|----|--\n  700   | 0  | 0  |\n  20    | 0  | 0  |\n  9     | 0  | 0  |\n```\nNow, we'll calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n1. The area of the rectangle formed by 900 and 700 is 900 \u00d7 700 = 630000\n2. The area of the rectangle formed by 900 and 20 is 900 \u00d7 20 = 18000\n3. The area of the rectangle formed by 900 and 9 is 900 \u00d7 9 = 8100\n4. The area of the rectangle formed by 60 and 700 is 60 \u00d7 700 = 42000\n5. The area of the rectangle formed by 60 and 20 is 60 \u00d7 20 = 1200\n6. The area of the rectangle formed by 60 and 9 is 60 \u00d7 9 = 540\n7. The area of the rectangle formed by 8 and 700 is 8 \u00d7 700 = 5600\n8. The area of the rectangle formed by 8 and 20 is 8 \u00d7 20 = 160\n9. The a