 numbers (loan amount and daily interest rate) is crucial in finance for determining the total interest accrued on a loan. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed examples. Can you provide another real-world scenario where the product of two numbers is used in a different field, such as in the field of transportation or energy?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Another context where the product of two numbers is crucial is in the field of transportation, specifically in calculating the total fuel consumption for a fleet of vehicles.\n\n### Transportation: Total Fuel Consumption for a Fleet\n\n**Scenario**: A transportation company has 952 delivery trucks, and each truck consumes 365 liters of fuel per 100 kilometers. The company aims to determine the total fuel consumption for all trucks in a month.\n\n**Calculation**:\n1. **Fuel Consumption by One Truck in 100 Kilometers**: Calculate the fuel consumption by one truck in 100 kilometers.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Fuel Consumption by One Truck in 100 Kilometers} = 365 \\text{ liters}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Fuel Consumption by One Truck in One Kilometer**: Calculate the fuel consumption by one truck in one kilometer.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Fuel Consumption by One Truck in One Kilometer} = \\frac{365 \\text{ liters}}{100 \\text{ kilometers}} = 3.65 \\text{ liters per kilometer}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total Distance Traveled by All Trucks in a Month**: Calculate the total distance traveled by all trucks in a month.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total Distance Traveled by All Trucks in a Month} = 952 \\times 365 \\text{ kilometers}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Fuel Consumption by All Trucks in a Month**: Calculate the total fuel consumption by all trucks in a month.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total Fuel Consumption by All Trucks in a Month} = 952 \\times 365 \\times 3.65 \\text{ liters}\n   \\]\n\nLet's perform the calculations step by step:\n\n1. **Total Distance Traveled by All Trucks in a Month**:\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 365 = 3456400 \\text{ kilometers}\n   \\]\