\n4. **Adding the Results:**\n   - Now, we add the three results together:\n     ```\n     1932\n   + 5520\n   +19320\n   -----\n   24672\n     ```\n\nSo, the final product of 276 and 727 is 24672.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nCertainly! Let's break down the multiplication of 276 by 727 step by step:\n\n1. **Multiplying by the Units Digit:**\n   - We start by multiplying 276 by 7 (the units digit of 727).\n   ```\n   276\n\u00d7   7\n-----\n 1932\n   ```\n   - This is done by multiplying 276 by 7:\n     ```\n     276\n   \u00d7   7\n   -----\n     1932\n     ```\n\n2. **Multiplying by the Tens Digit:**\n   - Next, we multiply 276 by 20 (the tens digit of 727, which is 2 times 10).\n   ```\n   276\n\u00d7  20\n-----\n 5520\n   ```\n   - This is done by multiplying 276 by 20:\n     ```\n     276\n   \u00d7  20\n   -----\n   5520\n     ```\n\n3. **Multiplying by the Hundreds Digit:**\n   - Finally, we multiply 276 by 700 (the hundreds digit of 727, which is 7 times 100).\n   ```\n   276\n\u00d7 700\n-----\n19320\n   ```\n   - This is done by multiplying 276 by 700:\n     ```\n     276\n   \u00d7 700\n   -----\n   19320\n     ```\n\n4. **Adding the Results:**\n   - Now, we add the three results together:\n     ```\n     1932\n   + 5520\n   +19320\n   -----\n   24672\n     ```\n\nSo, the final product of 276 and 727 is 24672.\n</answer>",
