s 3) \\times 100 \\]\n\\[ 643 \\times 3 = 1929 \\]\n\\[ 1929 \\times 100 = 192900 \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(643 \\times 2\\):\n\\[ 643 \\times 2 = 1286 \\]\n\nNow, add the two results together:\n\\[ 192900 + 1286 = 194186 \\]\n\nSo, using the distributive property, the product of 643 and 302 is:\n\\[ 643 \\times 302 = 194186 \\]\n\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into simpler multiplications and additions, making it easier to manage. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>That makes sense. Thank you for walking me through it.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any topic, feel free to ask. Understanding different methods can help solidify your knowledge and make solving problems more intuitive. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the area model?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nCertainly! The area model is a visual method that helps break down multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts. For the multiplication of 643 by 302, we can think of it as finding the area of a rectangle where one side is 643 and the other side is 302.\n\nHere's how we can set up the area model:\n\n1. Break down 302 into 300 and 2:\n\\[ 643 \\times 302 = 643 \\times (300 + 2) \\]\n\n2. Draw a rectangle and divide it into two smaller rectangles:\n   - One rectangle has one side as 643 and the other side as 300.\n   - The other rectangle has one side as 643 and the other side as 2.\n\n3. Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n   - The area of the first rectangle (643 \u00d7 300) is:\n     \\[\n     643 \\times 300 = 643 \\times (3 \\times 100) = (643 \\times 3) \\times 100\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     643 \\times 3 = 1929\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     1929 \\times 100 = 192900\n     \\]\n\n   - The area of the second rectangle (643 \u00d7 2) is:\n     \\[\n     643 \\times 2 = 1286\n     \\]\n\n4. Add the areas of the two smaller rectangles to get the total area:\n   \\[\n   192900 + 1286 = 194186\n   \\]\n\nSo, using the area model, the product of 643 and 302 is:\n\\[ 643 \\times 302 = 194186 \\]\n\nThis method visually represents the multiplication and helps in understanding the distributive property in a more concrete way. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation using the area model. It really helps to visualize the process.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! I'm glad you found the explanation helpful. The area model is a great way to visualize multiplication and can be very useful for understanding the underlying concepts. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any topic, feel free to ask. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the partial products method?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nCertainly! The partial products method is another way to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. It involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then summing the results. Let's solve \\(643 \\times 302\\) using the partial products method.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. **Break down the numbers into their place values:**\n   - \\(643 = 600 + 40 + 3\\)\n   - \\(302 = 300 + 2\\)\n\n2. **Multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:**\n   - \\(600 \\times 300\\)\n   - \\(600 \\times 2\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 300\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 2\\)\n   - \\(3 \\times 300\\)\n   - \\(3 \\times 2\\)\n\n3. **Calculate each product:**\n   - \\(600 \\times 300 = 180000\\)\n   - \\(600 \\times 2 = 1200\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 300 = 12000\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n   - \\(3 \\times 300 = 900\\)\n   - \\(3 \\times 2 = 6\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   180000 + 1200 + 12000 + 80 + 900 + 6 = 194186\n   \\]\n\nSo, using the partial products method, the product of 643 and 302 is:\n\\[ 643 \\times 302 = 194186 \\]\n\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts and then sums them up to get the fi