 and 979 as a sum of products of 983 with each digit of 979, shifted appropriately. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n<answer>\nCertainly! To verify the result using the distributive property of multiplication, we can express the product of 983 and 979 as a sum of products of 983 with each digit of 979, shifted appropriately. Let's break it down step by step.\n\nThe distributive property of multiplication states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). We can apply this property to break down the multiplication of 983 and 979 as follows:\n\n\\[983 \\times 979 = 983 \\times (900 + 70 + 9)\\]\n\nUsing the distributive property, we can expand this as:\n\n\\[983 \\times 979 = 983 \\times 900 + 983 \\times 70 + 983 \\times 9\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each term separately:\n\n1. **Calculate \\(983 \\times 900\\):**\n   \\[\n   983 \\times 900 = 983 \\times (9 \\times 100) = (983 \\times 9) \\times 100\n   \\]\n   We already know from our previous calculation that \\(983 \\times 9 = 8847\\), so:\n   \\[\n   983 \\times 900 = 8847 \\times 100 = 884700\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(983 \\times 70\\):**\n   \\[\n   983 \\times 70 = 983 \\times (7 \\times 10) = (983 \\times 7) \\times 10\n   \\]\n   We can calculate \\(983 \\times 7\\) as follows:\n   \\[\n   983 \\times 7 = 6881\n   \\]\n   So:\n   \\[\n   983 \\times 70 = 6881 \\times 10 = 68810\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate \\(983 \\times 9\\):**\n   \\[\n   983 \\times 9 = 8847\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum these results:\n\\[\n983 \\times 979 = 884700 + 68810 + 8847 = 965557\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 983 and 979 is indeed 965557, as we previously calculated. This verification confirms the accuracy of our result. <|User|>Thank you for the detailed explanation using the distributive property. Can you also show me how to verify the result using the long division method?\n<think>\nCertainly! To verify the result using the long division method, we can divide the product 965557 by 979 to see if we get 983 as