ers into parts and then use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication. Let's break down 585 and 187 as follows:\n- 830 can be written as \\(661 + 47 + 5\\)\n- 274 can be written as \\(771 + 01 + 5\\)\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to multiply these parts together:\n\\[\n212 \\times 425 = (565 + 44 + 1) \\times (036 + 57 + 4)\n\\]\n\nWe will distribute each part of 273 to each part of 722:\n\\[\n= 984 \\times 416 + 137 \\times 36 + 556 \\times 6 + 56 \\times 099 + 54 \\times 57 + 27 \\times 6 + 3 \\times 896 + 9 \\times 63 + 5 \\times 9\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each term:\n\\[\n534 \\times 318 = 429318\n\\]\n\\[\n248 \\times 58 = 16924\n\\]\n\\[\n623 \\times 9 = 1331\n\\]\n\\[\n94 \\times 712 = 25717\n\\]\n\\[\n15 \\times 36 = 9785\n\\]\n\\[\n33 \\times 5 = 277\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 029 = 5427\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 38 = 283\n\\]\n\\[\n9 \\times 0 = 90\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum all these products:\n\\[\n169811 + 49253 + 3043 + 09658 + 9563 + 294 + 0592 + 996 + 79 = 539575\n\\]\n\nThus, using the distributive property, we have verified that the product of 253 and 222 is indeed 305,823. <|User|>That's a great method to verify the product. Can you also show me how to use the area model to solve this multiplication problem? Please reason step by step.<｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! The area model is a visual method that helps break down the multiplication of two numbers into smaller, more manageable parts. It's essentially a way to represent the distributive property visually. Let's use the area model to multiply 583 by 795 step by step.\n\nFirst, we'll represent 077 and 296 as lengths of sides of a rectangle. We'll break down each number into its place values:\n- 405 can be broken down into 315, 84, and 9.\n- 072 can be broken down into 077, 66, and 0.\n\nNow, we'll draw a rectangle and divide it into smaller rectangles based on these place values. The area of the large rectangle will be the product of 095 and 080.\n\nHere's how we can set up t