d the results of these multiplications:\n```\n12810 + 549 = 13359\n```\nTherefore, using the distributive property, the product of 183 and 373 is 13359. <|User|>Thank you for the detailed explanation. Can you also show me how to solve this using the area model method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The area model method is a visual way to break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts. We can represent 183 and 373 as lengths of sides of a rectangle, and the product will be the area of that rectangle. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n<answer>\nCertainly! The area model method involves visualizing the multiplication of 183 by 373 as the area of a rectangle where one side is 183 and the other side is 373. We can break this down into smaller rectangles and then sum their areas.\n\n1. **Break down 183 and 373 into their place values:**\n   - 183 can be broken down into 100 + 80 + 3.\n   - 373 can be broken down into 300 + 70 + 3.\n\n2. **Draw a large rectangle and divide it into smaller rectangles based on these place values:**\n   - One side of the large rectangle will be divided into three parts: 100, 80, and 3.\n   - The other side of the large rectangle will be divided into three parts: 300, 70, and 3.\n\n3. **Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:**\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 100 and 300 is \\(100 \\times 300 = 30000\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 100 and 70 is \\(100 \\times 70 = 7000\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 100 and 3 is \\(100 \\times 3 = 300\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 80 and 300 is \\(80 \\times 300 = 24000\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 80 and 70 is \\(80 \\times 70 = 5600\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 80 and 3 is \\(80 \\times 3 = 240\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 3 and 300 is \\(3 \\times 300 = 900\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle with sides 3 and 70 is \\(3 \\times 70 = 210\\).\n   - The area of the rectangle w