00 + 15150 + 606 = 92758\nTherefore, the product of 303 and 352 is 92758. <|User|>That's helpful. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the area model?\n<think>\nCertainly! The area model is a visual method that helps break down multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts. For the problem 303 \u00d7 352, we can represent 303 as 300 + 3 and 352 as 300 + 50 + 2. Then, we can create a rectangle and divide it into smaller rectangles based on these factors. Let's set up the area model:\n```\n  300 |  3\n  300 |  50\n  300 |  2\n  3   |  3\n  3   |  50\n  3   |  2\n```\nNow, we'll calculate the area of each smaller rectangle and sum them up:\n1. 300 \u00d7 300 = 90000\n2. 300 \u00d7 50 = 15000\n3. 300 \u00d7 2 = 600\n4. 3 \u00d7 300 = 900\n5. 3 \u00d7 50 = 150\n6. 3 \u00d7 2 = 6\nAdding these areas together:\n90000 + 15000 + 600 + 900 + 150 + 6 = 106756\nTherefore, the product of 303 and 352 is 106756.\n...\n<answer>\nUsing the area model, we can represent the multiplication of 303 and 352 as a rectangle divided into smaller rectangles based on the factors:\n```\n  300 |  3\n  300 |  50\n  300 |  2\n  3   |  3\n  3   |  50\n  3   |  2\n```\nNow, we'll calculate the area of each smaller rectangle and sum them up:\n1. 300 \u00d7 300 = 90000\n2. 300 \u00d7 50 = 15000\n3. 300 \u00d7 2 = 600\n4. 3 \u00d7 300 = 900\n5. 3 \u00d7 50 = 150\n6. 3 \u00d7 2 = 6\nAdding these areas together:\n90000 + 15000 + 600 + 900 + 150 + 6 = 106756\nTherefore, the product of 303 and 352 is 106756. <|User|>This is very helpful. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the partial products method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The partial products method involves breaking down each number into its place values and then multiplying each part separately before summing the results. For the problem 303 \u00d7 352, we can break down 303 into 300 + 3 and 352 into 300 + 50 + 2. Then, we'll multiply each part and sum the results. Let's go through the steps:\n1. Multiply 300 by 300: