- \\( (4.5 \\times 10^4) \\times (2.3 \\times 10^2) \\)\n\n### Statistics\n1. **Mean, Median, and Mode**:\n   - Given the data set: \\( 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 \\)\n   - Calculate the mean, median, and mode.\n\n2. **Standard Deviation**:\n   - Given the data set: \\( 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 \\)\n   - Calculate the standard deviation.\n\n### Graphing\n1. **Graph a Function**:\n   - Graph the function \\( y = 2x + 3 \\) on the TI-30X Pro MathPrint.\n\n2. **Analyze a Graph**:\n   - Given the graph of \\( y = x^2 - 4x + 4 \\), identify the vertex, axis of symmetry, and intercepts.\n\n### Programming\n1. **Write a Simple Program**:\n   - Write a program to calculate the factorial of a number (e. g., \\( n! \\)).\n\n2. **Run a Program**:\n   - Run the program you wrote in the previous step to calculate \\( 5! \\).\n\n### Additional Resources\n- **TI-30X Pro MathPrint Practice Problems**:\n  - You can find practice problems and exercises on the Texas Instruments website: <https://education.ti.com/en/us/product/ti-30x-pro-mathprint-calculator/practice-problems>\n- **TI-30X Pro MathPrint Online Tutorials**:\n  - The Texas Instruments website also offers online tutorials and videos that can help you learn how to use the calculator effectively.\n\nBy working through these practice problems and exercises, you can become more comfortable with the **TI-30X Pro MathPrint** and its features. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Here are some practice problems and exercises that you can use to practice using the **TI-30X Pro MathPrint**:\n\n### Basic Arithmetic\n1. **Addition and Subtraction**:\n   - \\( 723 + 456 \\)\n   - \\( 987 - 345 \\)\n\n2. **Multiplication and Division**:\n   - \\( 123 \\times 45 \\)\n   - \\( 678 \\div 23 \\)\n\n3. **Mixed Operations**:\n   - \\( 567 + 89 \\times 23 - 45 \\)\n   - \\( (123 + 45) \\times (67 - 34) \\)\n\n### Fractions and Decimals\n1. **Fractions**:\n   - Convert \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\) to a decimal.\n   - Convert \\( 0.75 \\) to a fraction.\n\n2. **Decimal Opera