      "text": "318336. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you explain the process of finding the product of 664 and 988 using the distributive property of multiplication over addition?\n<think>\nCertainly! The distributive property of multiplication over addition allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. We can express 664 and 988 as sums of their digits and then distribute the multiplication over these sums. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n<answer>\nTo use the distributive property of multiplication over addition, we can express 664 and 988 as sums of their digits and then distribute the multiplication over these sums. Let's break it down:\n\nFirst, we can express 664 and 988 as:\n664 = 600 + 60 + 4\n988 = 900 + 80 + 8\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to multiply these sums:\n664 \u00d7 988 = (600 + 60 + 4) \u00d7 (900 + 80 + 8)\n\nWe can distribute the multiplication over each term:\n= (600 \u00d7 900) + (600 \u00d7 80) + (600 \u00d7 8) + (60 \u00d7 900) + (60 \u00d7 80) + (60 \u00d7 8) + (4 \u00d7 900) + (4 \u00d7 80) + (4 \u00d7 8)\n\nNow, let's calculate each of these products:\n= 540000 + 48000 + 480 + 54000 + 4800 + 480 + 3600 + 320 + 32\n\nNext, we'll sum these products:\n= 540000 + 48000 + 480 + 54000 + 4800 + 480 + 3600 + 320 + 32\n= 647920 + 480 + 480 + 3600 + 320 + 32\n= 647920 + 960 + 3600 + 320 + 32\n= 647920 + 13200 + 320 + 32\n= 647920 + 13520 + 32\n= 661440 + 32\n= 661472\n\nTherefore, the product of 664 and 988 is 661472.\n</answer>",
