ication algorithm?\n<think>\nCertainly! The standard long multiplication algorithm is a step-by-step method for multiplying two numbers. Here's how we can use it to multiply 228 and 449:\n\n1. Write the numbers one above the other, aligning the digits by place value.\n2. Multiply each digit of the bottom number by the rightmost digit of the top number, starting from the rightmost digit.\n3. Write the results in a new row, aligning the digits by place value.\n4. Shift the results one place to the left for each subsequent digit in the bottom number.\n5. Add all the resulting rows to get the final product.\n\nLet's set up the long multiplication:\n\n```\n    228\n  \u00d7 449\n  -----\n    228  (228 \u00d7 9)\n   892   (228 \u00d7 4, shifted one place to the left)\n  912   (228 \u00d7 40, shifted two places to the left)\n  -----\n  102372\n```\n\nNow, let's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Multiply 228 by 9:\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7   9\n   -----\n   2052\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 228 by 4 (shifted one place to the left):\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7  40\n   -----\n   9120\n   ```\n\n3. Multiply 228 by 400 (shifted two places to the left):\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7400\n   -----\n   91200\n   ```\n\n4. Add all the results:\n   ```\n   2052\n   9120\n   91200\n   -----\n   102372\n   ```\n\nTherefore, using the standard long multiplication algorithm, the product of 228 and 449 is 102,372.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're correct! The standard long multiplication algorithm is a reliable method for multiplying two numbers. Here's the step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. Write the numbers one above the other, aligning the digits by place value:\n```\n    228\n  \u00d7 449\n  -----\n```\n\n2. Multiply each digit of the bottom number by the rightmost digit of the top number (228 \u00d7 9):\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7   9\n   -----\n   2052\n   ```\n\n3. Multiply each digit of the bottom number by the next digit of the top number (228 \u00d7 4, shifted one place to the left):\n   ```\n  