      "text": "78643480857</\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>. However, this result seems incorrect as it's much larger than the expected product. Let's recheck the multiplication step by step:\n```\n   760\n\u00d7  798\n------\n  6080  (760 \u00d7 8)\n 60800  (760 \u00d7 90, shifted one place to the left)\n528000  (760 \u00d7 700, shifted two places to the left)\n------\n 60803480857\n```\nThe correct product of 760 and 798 is 60803480857. Therefore, the product of 402 and 843 is 3385446. </answer> <|User|>Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 402 and 843? Please reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we will use the standard multiplication algorithm. We'll start by writing the numbers one above the other:\n\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7 843\n  ------\n```\n\nWe'll multiply 402 by 3 (the units digit of 843), then by 40 (the tens digit of 843), and finally by 800 (the hundreds digit of 843). We'll need to shift the results of the second and third multiplications one and two places to the left, respectively.\n\n1. Multiply 402 by 3:\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7   3\n  ------\n    1206\n```\n\n2. Multiply 402 by 40 (which is 402 \u00d7 4):\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7   40\n  ------\n   16080\n```\nSince we are multiplying by the tens digit, we shift the result one place to the left:\n```\n   16080\n```\n\n3. Multiply 402 by 800 (which is 402 \u00d7 8):\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7  800\n  ------\n  321600\n```\nSince we are multiplying by the hundreds digit, we shift the result two places to the left:\n```\n  321600\n```\n\nNow, we add all these results together:\n```\n    1206\n  + 16080\n  +321600\n  ------\n  338546\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 402 and 843 is 338546.\n<|User|>Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 402 and 843? Please reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we will use the standard multiplication algorithm. We'll start by writing the numbers one above the other:\n\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7 843\n  ------\n```\n\nWe'll multiply 402 by 3 (the units digit of 843), then by 40 (the tens digit of 843), and finally by 800 (the hundreds digit of 843). We'll need to shift the results of the second and third multiplications one and two places to the left, respectively.\n\n1. Multiply 402 by 3:\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7   3\n  ------\n    1206\n```\n\n2. Multiply 402 by 40 (which is 402 \u00d7 4):\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7   40\n  ------\n   16080\n```\nSince we are multiplying by the tens digit, we shift the result one place to the left:\n```\n   16080\n```\n\n3. Multiply 402 by 800 (which is 402 \u00d7 8):\n```\n    402\n  \u00d7  800\n  ------\n  321600\n```\nSince we are multiplying by the hundreds digit, we shift the result two places to the left:\n```\n  321600\n```\n\nNow, we add all these results together:\n```\n    1206\n  + 16080\n  +321600\n  ------\n  338546\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 402 and 843 is 338546.\n</answer>",
