0d7 9 = 720\n   - 4 \u00d7 100 = 400\n   - 4 \u00d7 10 = 40\n   - 4 \u00d7 9 = 36\n\n5. Add all these areas together:\n60000 + 6000 + 5400 + 8000 + 800 + 720 + 400 + 40 + 36 = 75396\n\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 75396. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you also explain how to solve this problem using the partial products method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The partial products method involves breaking down each number into its place values and then multiplying each part separately. After finding the partial products, we add them together to get the final result. Let's apply this method to solve 684 \u00d7 119.\n\nFirst, let's break down 684 and 119 into their place values:\n684 = 600 + 80 + 4\n119 = 100 + 10 + 9\n\nNow, we'll multiply each part of 684 by each part of 119 and then add the results:\n1. 600 \u00d7 100 = 60000\n2. 600 \u00d7 10 = 6000\n3. 600 \u00d7 9 = 5400\n4. 80 \u00d7 100 = 8000\n5. 80 \u00d7 10 = 800\n6. 80 \u00d7 9 = 720\n7. 4 \u00d7 100 = 400\n8. 4 \u00d7 10 = 40\n9. 4 \u00d7 9 = 36\n\nNow, we'll add all these partial products together:\n60000 + 6000 + 5400 + 8000 + 800 + 720 + 400 + 40 + 36 = 75396\n\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 75396.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the partial products method, we can break down the multiplication of 684 and 119 into smaller, more manageable parts. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Break down 684 into its place values: 600, 80, and 4.\n2. Break down 119 into its place values: 100, 10, and 9.\n3. Multiply each part of 684 by each part of 119:\n   - 600 \u00d7 100 = 60000\n   - 600 \u00d7 10 = 6000\n   - 600 \u00d7 9 = 5400\n   - 80 \u00d7 100 = 8000\n   - 80 \u00d7 10 = 800\n   - 80 \u00d7 9 = 720\n   - 4 \u00d7 100 = 400\n   - 4 \u00d7 10 = 40\n   - 4 \u00d7 9 = 36\n4. Add all these partial products together:\n   60000 + 6000 + 5400 + 8000 + 800 + 720 + 400 + 40 + 36 = 75396\n\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 75396. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you also explain how to solve this problem using the lattice method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The lattice method is a visual and systematic way to multiply two numbers. Let's apply it to solve 684 \u00d7 119.\n\nFirst, we'll set up a lattice grid with the number of columns equal to the number of digits in the first number (684) and the number of rows equal to the number of digits in the second number (119). Since 684 has 3 digits and 119 has 3 digits, we'll have a 3x3 grid.\n\nHere's how the lattice grid will look:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nNow, we'll multiply each digit of the first number by each digit of the second number, placing the tens digit in the upper triangle and the ones digit in the lower triangle. We'll then add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary.\n\nLet's perform the multiplications:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nNow, let's fill in the grid:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nNext, we'll add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nThe final result, after adding the numbers in each diagonal, is:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 75396.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the lattice method, we can solve the multiplication of 684 and 119 as follows:\n\n1. Set up a 3x3 lattice grid, with the number of columns equal to the number of digits in 684 (3) and the number of rows equal to the number of digits in 119 (3).\n\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\n2. Multiply each digit of 684 by each digit of 119, placing the tens digit in the upper triangle and the ones digit in the lower triangle:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\n3. Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nThe final result, after adding the numbers in each diagonal, is:\n```\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n  6 | 8 | 4\n  - + - + -\n  1 | 1 | 9\n```\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 75396. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you also explain how to solve this problem using the standard long multiplication method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The standard long multiplication method involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number, starting from the rightmost digit, and then summing the results. Let's apply this method to solve 684 \u00d7 119.\n\nHere's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Write 684 and 119 one below the other, aligning the digits by place value:\n```\n  684\n\u00d7 119\n------\n```\n2. Multiply 684 by 9 (the units digit of 119):\n```\n  684\n\u00d7   9\n------\n 6156\n```\n3. Multiply 684 by 10 (the tens digit of 119), and remember to shift the result one place to the left:\n```\n  684\n\u00d7  10\n------\n 6840\n```\n4. Multiply 684 by 100 (the hundreds digit of 119), and remember to shift the result two places to the left:\n```\n  684\n\u00d7 100\n------\n 68400\n```\n5. Add the results of these multiplications:\n```\n  6156\n+ 6840\n+ 68400\n------\n 75396\n```\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 75396.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the standard long multiplication method, we can solve the problem as follows:\n\n1. Write 684 and 119 one below the other, aligning the digits by place value:\n```\n  684\n\u00d7 119\n------\