\uff5c>Could you also provide an example of how to solve this problem using the partial products method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The partial products method involves breaking down each number into its place values and then multiplying each part separately before summing the results. Let's break down the numbers 856 and 949 using the partial products method:\n\n1. Break down 856 into 800, 50, and 6.\n2. Break down 949 into 900, 40, and 9.\n3. Multiply each part of 856 by each part of 949 and then sum the results.\n\nLet's do the calculations step by step:\n\n1. Multiply 800 by 900:\n   ```\n   800\n   \u00d7 900\n   -----\n   720000\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 800 by 40:\n   ```\n   800\n   \u00d7 40\n   -----\n   32000\n   ```\n\n3. Multiply 800 by 9:\n   ```\n   800\n   \u00d7  9\n   -----\n   7200\n   ```\n\n4. Multiply 50 by 900:\n   ```\n   50\n   \u00d7 900\n   -----\n   45000\n   ```\n\n5. Multiply 50 by 40:\n   ```\n   50\n   \u00d7 40\n   -----\n   2000\n   ```\n\n6. Multiply 50 by 9:\n   ```\n   50\n   \u00d7  9\n   -----\n   450\n   ```\n\n7. Multiply 6 by 900:\n   ```\n   6\n   \u00d7 900\n   -----\n   5400\n   ```\n\n8. Multiply 6 by 40:\n   ```\n   6\n   \u00d7 40\n   -----\n   240\n   ```\n\n9. Multiply 6 by 9:\n   ```\n   6\n   \u00d7  9\n   -----\n   54\n   ```\n\nNow, sum all these partial products:\n```\n720000 + 32000 + 7200 + 45000 + 2000 + 450 + 5400 + 240 + 54 = 776344\n```\n\nSo, the product of 856 and 949 is 776344.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the partial products method, we can break down the multiplication of 856 and 949 as follows:\n\n1. Break down 856 into 800, 50, and 6.\n2. Break down 949 into 900, 40, and 9.\n3. Multiply each part of 856 by each part of 949 and then sum the results:\n\n- Multiply 800 by 900:\n  ```\n  800\n  \u00d7 900\n  -----\n  720000\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 800 by 40:\n  ```\n  800\n  \u00d7 40\n  -----\n  32000\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 800 by 9:\n  ```\n  800\n  \u00d7  9\n  -----\n  7200\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 50 by 900:\n  ```\n  50\n  \u00d7 900\n  -----\n  45000\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 50 by 40:\n  ```\n  50\n  \u00d7 40\n  -----\n  2000\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 50 by 9:\n  ```\n  50\n  \u00d7  9\n  -----\n  450\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 6 by 900:\n  ```\n  6\n  \u00d7 900\n  -----\n  5400\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 6 by 40:\n  ```\n  6\n  \u00d7 40\n  -----\n  240\n  ```\n\n- Multiply 6 by 9:\n  ```\n  6\n  \u00d7  9\n  -----\n  54\n  ```\n\nNow, sum all these partial products:\n```\n720000 + 32000 + 7200 + 45000 + 2000 + 450 + 5400 + 240 + 54 = 776344\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 856 and 949 is 776344. Thank you for asking about the partial products method; it's a useful technique for breaking down multiplication into simpler steps. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you also provide an example of how to solve this problem using the standard long multiplication algorithm?\n<think>\nCertainly! The standard long multiplication algorithm involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number, starting from the rightmost digit, and then summing the results. Let's solve the problem of multiplying 856 by 949 using the standard long multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Write the numbers one below the other:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7 949\n```\n\n2. Multiply 856 by 9 (the units digit of 949):\n```\n  856\n\u00d7   9\n-----\n  7704\n```\n\n3. Multiply 856 by 4 (the tens digit of 949), and remember to shift one place to the left:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7  40\n-----\n 34240\n```\n\n4. Multiply 856 by 9 (the hundreds digit of 949), and remember to shift two places to the left:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7 900\n-----\n 770400\n```\n\n5. Now, add all the results together:\n```\n   7704\n+ 34240\n+ 770400\n-----\n 776344\n```\n\nSo, the product of 856 and 949 is 776344.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the standard long multiplication algorithm, we can solve the problem of multiplying 856 by 949 as follows:\n\n1. Write the numbers one below the other:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7 949\n```\n\n2. Multiply 856 by 9 (the units digit of 949):\n```\n  856\n\u00d7   9\n-----\n  7704\n```\n\n3. Multiply 856 by 4 (the tens digit of 949), and remember to shift one place to the left:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7  40\n-----\n 34240\n```\n\n4. Multiply 856 by 9 (the hundreds digit of 949), and remember to shift two places to the left:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7 900\n-----\n 770400\n```\n\n5. Now, add all the results together:\n```\n   7704\n+ 34240\n+ 770400\n-----\n 776344\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 856 and 949 is 776344. Thank you for asking about the standard long multiplication algorithm; it's a reliable method for solving multiplication problems. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you also provide an example of how to solve this problem using the lattice method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The lattice method is an alternative way to perform multiplication using a grid. Here's how we can solve the problem of multiplying 856 by 949 using the lattice method:\n\n1. Draw a 2x2 grid (since 856 has 3 digits and 949 has 3 digits, we need a 2x2 grid).\n2. Write the digits of 856 along the top of the grid and the digits of 949 along the right side of the grid.\n3. Multiply each digit of the top row by each digit of the right column, and write the results in the corresponding cells of the grid, splitting the tens and units digits.\n4. Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary.\n5. Read the final product from the bottom and right edges of the grid.\n\nLet's go through the steps:\n\n1. Draw a 2x2 grid:\n```\n  856\n\u00d7 949\n-----\n```\n\n2. Write the digits along the top and right side:\n```\n  8 | 5 | 6\n\u00d7 9 | 4 | 9\n-----\n```\n\n3. Multiply each digit and write the results in the grid:\n```\n  8 | 5 | 6\n\u00d7 9 | 4 | 9\n-----\n  72 | 40 | 54\n  360 | 200 | 540\n  720 | 200 | 540\n-----\n```\n\n4. Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary:\n```\n  72 | 40 | 54\n+ 360 | 200 | 540\n+ 720 | 200 | 540\n-----\n  776 | 340 | 540\n```\n\n5. Read the final product from the bottom and right edges of th