o the left:**\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7 200\n   -----\n   45600\n   ```\n\n5. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7 241\n   -----\n   53208\n   ```\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown with a Different Carrying Process:\n\n1. **First Multiplication:**\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7  1\n   -----\n   228\n   ```\n\n2. **Second Multiplication:**\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7  40\n   -----\n   9120\n   ```\n\n   - Multiply 228 by 4:\n     ```\n     228\n     \u00d7  4\n     -----\n     912\n     ```\n   - Shift the result one place to the left:\n     ```\n     228\n     \u00d7  40\n     -----\n     9120\n     ```\n\n3. **Third Multiplication:**\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7 200\n   -----\n   45600\n   ```\n\n   - Multiply 228 by 2:\n     ```\n     228\n     \u00d7  2\n     -----\n     456\n     ```\n   - Shift the result two places to the left:\n     ```\n     228\n     \u00d7 200\n     -----\n     45600\n     ```\n\n4. **Adding the Intermediate Results:**\n   ```\n   228\n   \u00d7 241\n   -----\n   53208\n   ```\n\n   - Add the results of the three multiplications:\n     ```\n     228\n     \u00d7 241\n     -----\n     53208\n     ```\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown with the Partial Products Method:\n\n1. **Break down 228 and 241 into their place values:**\n   \\[\n   228 = 200 + 20 + 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   241 = 200 + 40 + 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply each part of 228 by each part of 241, filling in the grid with the products:**\n   ```\n   200 | 20 | 8\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n   200 | 0 | 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n   40  | 0 | 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n   1   | 0 | 0 |\n   ```\n\n3. **Add up all the numbers in the grid, carrying over if necessary:**\n   ```\n   200 | 20 | 8\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n   200 | 0 | 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u