ht side of the grid.\n\n   ```\n       1  1  7\n     \u00d7  5  6  3\n       ------\n   ```\n\n2. **Divide each cell in the grid into two triangles:**\n   - Multiply the digit at the top of each column by the digit at the right of each row.\n   - Write the tens digit in the top triangle and the units digit in the bottom triangle.\n\n   ```\n       1  1  7\n     \u00d7  5  6  3\n       ------\n     5  6  3\n     6  6  9\n     7  7  2\n       ------\n   ```\n\n3. **Add the numbers in each diagonal:**\n   - Start from the bottom right and move to the top left.\n   - If the sum is a single digit, write it down.\n   - If the sum is a two-digit number, write the units digit and carry the tens digit to the next diagonal.\n\n   ```\n       1  1  7\n     \u00d7  5  6  3\n       ------\n     5  6  3\n     6  6  9\n     7  7  2\n       ------\n     6  4  8  5  1\n   ```\n\nTherefore, the product of 117 and 563 using the lattice method is 64851. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation using the lattice method. It's very helpful to see an alternative approach.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! The lattice method provides a visual and systematic way to multiply numbers, which can be particularly helpful for understanding the process. If you have any more questions or need further explanations, feel free to ask. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the grid method?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nCertainly! The grid method, also known as the box method, is a visual approach to multiplication that breaks down the numbers into smaller parts and then multiplies these parts. Let's solve \\(117 \\times 563\\) using the grid method step by step.\n\n1. **Set up the grid:**\n   - Break down 117 into 100, 10, and 7.\n   - Break down 563 into 500, 60, and 3.\n   - Draw a 3x3 grid and label the rows and columns with these parts.\n\n   ```\n       100 | 10 |  7\n     \u00d7  500 | 60 |  3\n       ------\n       500 | 60 |  3\n       600 | 60 |  3\n       700 | 70 |  21\n       ------\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply each part:**\n   - Multiply each row by each column and write the result in the corresponding cell.\n\n   ```\n       100 | 10 |  7\n     \u00d7  500 | 60 |  3\n       ------\n       50000 | 6000 |  21\n       6000 | 600 |  30\n       700 | 70 |  21\n       ------\n   ```\n\n3. **Add the numbers in each row:**\n   - Add the numbers in each row to get the final product.\n\n   ```\n       50000 | 6000 |  21\n     + 6000 | 600 |  30\n     + 700 | 70 |  21\n       ------\n       56700 | 670 |  72\n       ------\n   ```\n\nTherefore, the product of 117 and 563 using the grid method is 64851. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation using the grid method. It's very helpful to see an alternative approach.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! The grid method is a visual and systematic way to multiply numbers, breaking them down into smaller parts and then summing the results. If you have any more questions or need further explanations, feel free to ask. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the column method?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nCertainly! The column method is the standard way to multiply numbers by aligning them vertically by place value and then multiplying each digit step by step. Let's solve \\(117 \\times 563\\) using the column method step by step.\n\n1. **Write the numbers one above the other:**\n   ```\n     117\n   \u00d7 563\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply 117 by 3 (the units digit of 563):**\n   ```\n     117\n   \u00d7  3\n   -----\n     351\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply 117 by 60 (the tens digit of 563, which is 6 times 10):**\n   ```\n     117\n   \u00d7 60\n   -----\n    7020\n   ```\n\n4. **Multiply 117 by 500 (the hundreds digit of 563, which is 5 times 100):**\n   ```\n     117\n   \u00d7500\n   -----\n  58500\n   ```\n\n5. **Add the results of each step:**\n   ```\n     351\n   +7020\n   +58500\n   -----\n  64851\n   ```\n\nTherefore, the prod