all the terms:\n   200000 + 10000 + 1000 + 32000 + 1600 + 160 + 3200 + 160 + 16 = 247136\n\nTherefore, the product of 588 and 422 using the distributive property is 247136.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the distributive property of multiplication over addition, we can express the multiplication of 588 and 422 as follows:\n\n1. Break down 588 and 422 into their components:\n   588 = 500 + 80 + 8\n   422 = 400 + 20 + 2\n\n2. Apply the distributive property:\n   (500 + 80 + 8) \u00d7 (400 + 20 + 2) = 500 \u00d7 400 + 500 \u00d7 20 + 500 \u00d7 2 + 80 \u00d7 400 + 80 \u00d7 20 + 80 \u00d7 2 + 8 \u00d7 400 + 8 \u00d7 20 + 8 \u00d7 2\n\n3. Calculate each term:\n   500 \u00d7 400 = 200000\n   500 \u00d7 20 = 10000\n   500 \u00d7 2 = 1000\n   80 \u00d7 400 = 32000\n   80 \u00d7 20 = 1600\n   80 \u00d7 2 = 160\n   8 \u00d7 400 = 3200\n   8 \u00d7 20 = 160\n   8 \u00d7 2 = 16\n\n4. Sum all the terms:\n   200000 + 10000 + 1000 + 32000 + 1600 + 160 + 3200 + 160 + 16 = 247136\n\nTherefore, the product of 588 and 422 using the distributive property is 247136. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>The explanation is clear. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the long multiplication method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The long multiplication method involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number, starting from the rightmost digit, and then summing the results. Let's solve the problem 588 \u00d7 422 using the long multiplication method step by step.\n\n1. Write the numbers one below the other:\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7 422\n  ------\n```\n\n2. Multiply 588 by 2 (the units digit of 422):\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7   2\n  ------\n    1176\n```\n3. Multiply 588 by 20 (the tens digit of 422, which is 2 times 10):\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7  20\n  ------\n   11760\n```\n4. Multiply 588 by 400 (the hundreds digit of 422, which is 4 times 100):\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7 400\n  ------\n  235200\n```\n\n5. Now, add all these results together:\n```\n    1176\n  +11760\n  +235200\n  ------\n  247136\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 588 and 422 using the long multiplication method is 247136.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Using the long multiplication method, we can solve the problem as follows:\n\n1. Write the numbers one below the other:\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7 422\n  ------\n```\n\n2. Multiply 588 by 2 (the units digit of 422):\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7   2\n  ------\n    1176\n```\n\n3. Multiply 588 by 20 (the tens digit of 422, which is 2 times 10):\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7  20\n  ------\n   11760\n```\n\n4. Multiply 588 by 400 (the hundreds digit of 422, which is 4 times 100):\n```\n    588\n  \u00d7 400\n  ------\n  235200\n```\n\n5. Now, add all these results together:\n```\n    1176\n  +11760\n  +235200\n  ------\n  247136\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 588 and 422 using the long multiplication method is 247136. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the lattice method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The lattice method is an alternative way to perform multiplication using a grid. Here's how we can solve the problem 588 \u00d7 422 using the lattice method:\n\n1. Draw a 2x2 grid (since 588 has 3 digits and 422 has 3 digits, the grid will have 2 rows and 2 columns).\n2. Write the digits of 588 along the top of the grid and the digits of 422 along the right side of the grid.\n3. Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the right column, and write the results in the corresponding cells of the grid, splitting the tens and units digits.\n4. Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary.\n5. The final product is read from the bottom and right edges of the grid.\n\nLet's go through the steps:\n\n1. Draw a 2x2 grid:\n```\n  5 | 8 | 8\n  - + - + -\n  4 | 2 | 2\n```\n\n2. Write the digits of 588 along the top and the digits of 422 along the right side:\n```\n  5 | 8 | 8\n  - + - + -\n  4 | 2 | 2\n```\n\n3. Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the righ